From 6b2236645ed4148951653b01c662b8e8284642fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snarayana <snarayana@student.ethz.ch>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:37:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: vllm fast weight loading (servekit launch -- vllm
 serve ...)

The roadmap's "Support vllm fast weight loading": presharding with vLLM's
own sharded_state, per-node sliced staging into /dev/shm, --overlap, and
the manifest checks, for `vllm serve MODEL` and `--model MODEL`.

- Command reading: the positional model (it wins over --model, as in vLLM),
  -tp/-pp, and the multiprocessing backend's --nnodes/--node-rank/
  --master-addr. vLLM's pipeline files are model-pp-{pp}-tp-{tp}, not
  SGLang's -rank-, so shard_glob takes the engine.
- prepare: a vLLM sharder (adapted from vLLM's save_sharded_state example)
  that takes every `vllm serve` flag, forces eager mode and one data-parallel
  replica, and skips stale *.index.json. A follower node serves headless
  until the head writes the manifest; vLLM's save RPC already waits for every
  worker, so no done-markers are needed.
- launch: --served-model-name is pinned to the original path, or vLLM would
  rename the model to /dev/shm/servekit/<name> for every client. Under
  --overlap, shards are staged into a hidden directory and renamed in when
  complete, so an engine without the barrier cannot read a half-written file.
  A headless worker node frees its copy once every local rank recorded its load.
- A vLLM plugin (vllm.general_plugins, inert unless servekit launched the
  engine) replaces the class behind `sharded_state` with a subclass that
  waits on the stage barrier, turns ShardedStateLoader's narrowing and
  dtype-cast warnings into errors (a TP-mismatched checkpoint otherwise
  serves wrong weights), and records each rank's load time, since vLLM logs
  "Model loading took" on local rank 0 only.
- vllm_guard: quantized checkpoints, MLA, expert parallelism, LoRA and
  speculative decoding are served on vLLM's own loader, not presharded:
  ShardedStateLoader reruns process_weights_after_loading on post-processed
  weights, and MLA registers W_UV/W_UK_T after loading. Ray-placed ranks
  likewise, since servekit cannot map them to nodes. A manifest from another
  vLLM minor version is a mismatch.
- Compile caches: VLLM_CACHE_ROOT and TileLang join the JIT caches in a
  separate module. They are written back beside the checkpoint after the
  first launch, because vLLM's cache key includes the served model path.
  servekit never sets VLLM_PLUGINS, which vLLM hashes into that key.

Tests: tests/test_vllm.py (59) with a fake sharder, a fake engine, the plugin
against a stand-in vllm package, and one end-to-end --overlap run through a
mock `vllm serve` subprocess behind the real run_profile. Nothing has run on
a GPU yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
